engine#315 — the REFUTED candidate fix, preserved as evidence (do NOT land)

HYPOTHESIS (refuted 2026-10-13 by its own pre-registered A/B, commit fc7ffd5):
  buffer_get() read a host-visible, NON-COHERENT mmap with a bare memcpy, and no cache-invalidate
  exists on that path, so the CPU could observe a stale view of the logits allocation.

TEST RESULT (commit f84be10):
  ARM A  GGML_HRX_COHERENT_READ unset : cell e OK=0 FAULT=4   <- 4 of 4 eviction arms faulted
  ARM B  GGML_HRX_COHERENT_READ=1     : cell e faults too (Face B, http=1 s500=1 unparsed=2)
  => the fix does NOT reduce the eviction-cell fault rate. The read path is not where the
     corruption enters.

WHY IT IS PRESERVED: it is the record of a mechanism hypothesis that was killed by experiment rather
than argument, and its failure is a real constraint on the remaining candidate space (it removes the
entire read side, leaving the write side and intermediate-buffer propagation).

--- The change, as built and tested (patched tree ~/wt/llama-315coherent, build ~/wt/315coherent-build) ---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hrx/ggml-hrx.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hrx/ggml-hrx.cpp
@@ buffer_get(ggml_backend_buffer_t buffer, const ggml_tensor * tensor, void * data,
@@            size_t offset, size_t size)
     GGML_ASSERT(source_offset <= buffer->size && size <= buffer->size - source_offset);
+    // engine#315 (REFUTED CANDIDATE): a host-visible buffer is mmap'd non-coherently
+    // (HRX_MEMORY_TYPE_HOST_LOCAL | DEVICE_VISIBLE = 0x52, no HOST_COHERENT) and the runtime exposes no
+    // cache-invalidate call, so a bare memcpy can hand back the CPU's stale view of the mapping rather
+    // than what the device wrote. Route the read through the runtime's own device-to-host transfer.
+    // Gated so an A/B stays one binary; off by default.
+    if (environment_flag_enabled("GGML_HRX_COHERENT_READ")) {
+        if (!HRX_CHECK(hrx_synchronous_d2h(context->device->device, context->buffer, source_offset, data, size))) {
+            GGML_LOG_ERROR("%s: HRX buffer download failed\n", __func__);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
     if (context->base != reinterpret_cast<uint8_t *>(GGML_HRX_FAKE_PTR_BASE)) {
         std::memcpy(data, context->base + source_offset, size);
         return;
     }
